// TestOpenCodeResumedSessionAfterCommit verifies that resuming an OpenCode session
// after a commit correctly creates a checkpoint for the second turn.
//
// This tests the scenario:
//  1. Turn 1: create new file → checkpoint → user commits (condensation)
//  2. Turn 2 (resumed): modify the now-tracked file → checkpoint should be created
//
// Bug: transcript-based file extraction used "file_path" key but OpenCode exports use
// "filePath" (camelCase). Turn 1 worked because the file was NEW (detected via git status).
// Turn 2 failed because the file was now tracked+modified — only detectable via transcript
// extraction, which silently returned empty due to the key mismatch.

